	('1f4ee6a1-4d55-435e-935e-a6ad1641144f', '38dd0c32-6e6c-4222-b61d-4f8710630984', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-30', '49 -PINK APARTMENT PASCHIM VIHAR', NULL, 1100.00, 'SQ_FT', 'NORTH', 'Yes', NULL, 1, 0, 'FLAT', 'EXISTING_VACANT', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '•	LIVING ROOM\n•	KITCHEN\n•	MASTER BEDROOM\n•	MASTER WASHROOM\n•	KIDS BEDROOM\n•	PARENTS BEDROOM \n•	COMMON WASHROOM\n•	LOBBY AREA\n•	BALCONY\n \n', NULL, 'Some civil and demolition work done by their  mahesh ji [ civil contractor ]', 'yes , as per vastu consultant ', 'as per vastu consultant ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'as per vastu consultant ', 'HIGH', NULL, 'INR', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, '21252981-f16a-4c36-a445-f3bf76d88b06', '2026-10-30', NULL, NULL, 'DRAFT', 1, '2026-10-30 11:15:37', '2026-11-21 13:00:19', '2026-11-21 13:00:19', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'RESIDENTIAL', NULL, NULL),
	('52982cc4-38a2-445d-be35-c5b31716a9a8', 'c4a41869-a229-4bbb-bc90-83bcfe6f68f1', 'FRIEND', 'Architectural Referral – Existing Client Recommendation (Word of Mouth).', '2026-11-15', 'B-Block, Sector 15, Gurugram, Haryana – 122001, India.', '47c269f2-7e6b-11f1-b721-52540021303b', 4000.00, 'SQ_FT', 'NORTH_EAST', 'Yes', 'OWNED', 5, 1, 'BUILDER_FLOOR', 'COLD_SHELL', 'STRUCTURAL', 'hi', NULL, NULL, '- Entrance Foyer & Main Lobby\n- Formal Living Room\n- Family Lounge\n- Dining Area\n- Modular Kitchen & Utility\n- Master Bedroom with Walk-in Wardrobe\n- 2 Guest Bedrooms\n- Kids’ Bedroom\n- Attached Bathrooms\n- Powder Room\n- Internal Staircase & Upper Landing\n- Balcony & Terrace Seating\n- Wardrobes, Storage & Custom Furniture\n- Lighting, Ceiling & Interior Finishes', '- Structural modifications and major civil construction\n- External façade redesign and elevation work\n- Landscaping and outdoor garden development\n- Boundary wall, gate and driveway construction\n- Swimming pool and water-feature installations\n- Home automation and security system integration\n- HVAC and centralized air-conditioning systems\n- Solar panel and renewable energy installations\n- External plumbing and drainage infrastructure\n- Loose décor accessories and artwork procurement (unless separately commissioned)\n', '- Architectural floor plans and initial space planning completed by the appointed architect.\n- Structural design and foundation work completed by the civil contractor.\n- Primary brickwork and internal partition walls completed.\n- Electrical conduits and initial plumbing provisions installed.\n- External façade and building elevation completed.\n- Aluminium window frames and glazing installed.\n- Basic plastering and initial surface preparation completed.\n- Main entrance door and external staircase completed.', '- Main entrance preferred in the North or East direction, maintaining a bright and welcoming entryway.\n- Master bedroom preferably located in the South-West zone for stability and privacy.\n- Kitchen ideally positioned in the South-East direction, with the cooking hob facing East.\n- Pooja room to be located in the North-East zone, with provision for a compact dedicated prayer space.\n- Living and formal entertaining areas preferably oriented towards the North or East for natural light.\n- Dining area positioned adjacent to the kitchen with comfortable circulation.\n- Children\'s bedrooms preferably in the West or North-West zones.\n- Grandmother\'s bedroom to prioritize ground-floor accessibility, comfort and natural ventilation.\n- Staircase preferably located in the South, West or South-West zone.\n- Toilets and bathrooms preferably positioned in the West or North-West zones, avoiding the North-East.\n- Adequate natural lighting, cross-ventilation and unobstructed circulation throughout the residence.\n- Avoid excessive dark finishes in the North-East zone and maintain a clean, uncluttered prayer area.', '- Bright neon shades such as fluorescent green, orange and pink.\n- Excessive use of deep red and bright yellow.\n- Harsh pure white across large surfaces.\n- Overwhelming black or very dark charcoal finishes.\n- Highly saturated purple and electric blue.\n- Excessive glossy gold and chrome finishes.\n- Busy multicolour patterns and high-contrast combinations.\n- Artificial-looking wood tones and overly reddish laminates.\n\nOverall Preference: Avoid overly loud, flashy or visually cluttered colour schemes. Maintain a warm, balanced and understated luxury aesthetic.', '- Natural Stone: Italian marble, Travertine, Botticino marble and premium quartzite.\n- Wood Finishes: Natural walnut veneer, smoked oak, teak and fluted wooden panels.\n- Wall Finishes: Textured paint, limewash, microcement and subtle decorative wall panelling.\n- Metal Finishes: Brushed brass, antique bronze and champagne-finish metal.\n- Flooring: Large-format marble, engineered wood and premium porcelain tiles.\n- Glass: Fluted glass, smoked glass and clear toughened glass.\n- Upholstery: Premium linen, velvet, bouclé and textured cotton fabrics.\n- Decorative Elements: Natural stone cladding, cane detailing, leather accents and handcrafted accessories.\n- Ceiling Materials: Gypsum false ceilings with concealed lighting and selected wooden detailing.\n\nOverall Preference: Natural, tactile and premium materials with subtle textures, refined detailing and long-lasting finishes. Prioritize durability, ease of maintenance and timeless appeal over excessive ornamentation.', '- High-gloss laminate and excessively reflective acrylic finishes.\n- Artificial marble sheets and low-quality stone imitations.\n- Cheap-looking PVC wall panels and decorative cladding.\n- Excessive use of plastic-based decorative materials.\n- Highly polished chrome and mirror-finish metallic surfaces.\n- Heavy, ornate carvings and overly traditional wooden detailing.\n- Artificial wood laminates with prominent reddish or yellowish tones.\n- Cheap glossy ceramic tiles with repetitive printed patterns.\n- Rough, unfinished concrete textures across large interior surfaces.\n- Low-grade upholstery fabrics that are difficult to maintain.\n- Excessive use of mirrored surfaces and reflective glass.\n- Delicate materials requiring frequent maintenance or specialized cleaning.\n\nOverall Preference: Avoid synthetic-looking, excessively glossy, low-durability and visually overpowering materials. The client prefers authentic finishes, refined craftsmanship, understated detailing and practical long-term maintenance.', '- Grand entrance foyer with a statement console, designer mirror and concealed shoe storage.\n- Dedicated pooja room with elegant marble detailing and warm ambient lighting.\n- Spacious formal living room with premium seating and a feature marble or stone TV wall.\n- Custom-designed 8-seater dining area with a statement chandelier.\n- Modular kitchen with a functional island counter, breakfast seating and integrated appliances.\n- Walk-in wardrobe with dedicated accessory, footwear and luggage storage in the master suite.\n- Dedicated home office with ergonomic workstations and video-conferencing provisions.\n- Layered lighting throughout, including cove lighting, accent lighting and decorative fixtures.\n- Customized wardrobes and concealed storage solutions across all bedrooms.\n- Smart lighting controls, video doorbell and centralized home networking provisions.\n- Grandmother-friendly bedroom and accessible bathroom with safety fittings.\n- Premium bathroom fittings with walk-in showers and floating vanities.\n- Dedicated display shelving for collectibles, family photographs and curated décor.\n- Balcony seating with greenery and weather-resistant furniture.\n- Terrace entertainment lounge for family gatherings.\n- Acoustic considerations and concealed wiring for entertainment systems.\n\nOverall Expectation: A thoughtfully planned contemporary luxury home that combines aesthetics, functionality, comfort, technology and personalized family spaces.', '- Primary Palette: Warm ivory, champagne beige, soft greige and off-white.\n- Secondary Palette: Taupe, muted olive green and warm mocha.\n- Wood Finishes: Natural walnut, smoked oak and light teak.\n- Accent Colours: Antique brass, brushed gold and subtle charcoal.\n- Soft Furnishings: Sand, oatmeal, muted sage and warm grey.\n- Bedrooms: Soft pastels, dusty blue, blush beige and muted lavender, customized to individual preferences.\n- Bathrooms: White marble, beige stone and subtle grey veining.\n\nOverall Theme: Contemporary Luxury with Warm Minimalism — timeless neutrals, natural textures, understated metallic accents and a calm, sophisticated ambience.', 'HIGH', 150000000.00, 'INR', NULL, '2026-12-15', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'The Malhotra family comprises a multi-generational household with a preference for contemporary luxury, functionality and comfortable everyday living. The family frequently hosts social gatherings, festive celebrations and weekend dinners, making spacious common areas and a well-planned dining space important priorities.\n\nThe interiors should reflect a sophisticated yet welcoming aesthetic, incorporating warm neutral palettes, natural stone, wood finishes, subtle metallic accents and layered lighting.\n\nSpecial consideration should be given to the grandmother\'s accessibility and comfort requirements, while providing personalized spaces for the younger family members. Ample concealed storage, efficient circulation, privacy between private and common zones, and practical housekeeping provisions are key planning considerations.', 'The finalization of the interior design direction, detailed space planning and room-wise material specifications is pending client approval. The exact site orientation and Vastu alignment need to be verified against the approved architectural drawings. Final confirmation is also required for the kitchen layout, appliance specifications, home automation requirements, lighting preferences and customized furniture details. The client is yet to finalize the overall project budget, preferred vendor selections and procurement priorities. Society renovation NOC, refundable security deposit, contractor registration and permitted work schedules must be confirmed before execution. Additionally, final site measurements, electrical and plumbing provisions, HVAC coordination, material availability and execution dependencies need to be reviewed before freezing the technical drawings and commencing on-site work.', '0ffc53c1-7213-11f1-8bb6-52540021303b', '2026-11-15', NULL, NULL, 'DRAFT', 2, '2026-11-15 06:39:41', '2026-11-23 11:24:20', '2026-11-23 11:24:20', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '3-6 months', NULL, 'RESIDENTIAL', NULL, NULL),
	('f82104f8-3477-4530-9e29-3b0604dee9bd', 'b462b69b-d9b8-45db-b495-6ad19ecc61ad', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-23', 'Pink Apartments, Paschim vihar , Delhi 110087', '47c269f2-7e6b-11f1-b721-52540021303b', 1100.00, 'SQ_FT', 'NORTH', 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 0, 'FLAT', 'COLD_SHELL', 'NONE', NULL, NULL, NULL, '• LIVING ROOM\n• KITCHEN\n• MASTER BEDROOM\n• MASTER WASHROOM\n• KIDS BEDROOM\n• PARENTS BEDROOM\n• COMMON WASHROOM\n• LOBBY AREA\n• BALCONY', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'According to vastu', 'MEDIUM', 3500000.00, 'INR', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, '0ffc53c1-7213-11f1-8bb6-52540021303b', '2026-11-23', NULL, NULL, 'SIGNED_OFF', 1, '2026-11-23 12:04:00', '2026-11-24 13:48:13', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '3-6 months', NULL, 'RESIDENTIAL', NULL, NULL);
